{"name":"Currywurst","hex":"#ddaa33","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"currywurst","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A German national dish consisting of hot pork sausage cut into slices and seasoned with curry ketchup."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/currywurst"}],"entries":[{"title":"Currywurst","blocks":[{"text":"Currywurst is a fast food dish of German origin consisting of sausage with curry ketchup. It was invented in 1949 by Herta Heuwer, who began selling it at a food stand in West Berlin. The Deutsches Currywurst Museum estimated that 800 million currywursts are eaten every year in Germany, with 70 million in Berlin alone."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/20220430_currywurst.jpg/330px-20220430_currywurst.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Currywurst"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Berlin_Konnopke%E2%80%99s_Imbi%C3%9F.jpg/500px-Berlin_Konnopke%E2%80%99s_Imbi%C3%9F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Berlin_Konnopke%E2%80%99s_Imbi%C3%9F.jpg/1280px-Berlin_Konnopke%E2%80%99s_Imbi%C3%9F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Berlin_Konnopke%E2%80%99s_Imbi%C3%9F.jpg/500px-Berlin_Konnopke%E2%80%99s_Imbi%C3%9F.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Konnopke's Imbiss (Fast Food Stand) in Berlin. It was the first Imbiss to sell currywurst in East-Berlin in 1960.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABerlin_Konnopke%E2%80%99s_Imbi%C3%9F.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Currywurst_med_toast_%284541065102%29.jpg/120px-Currywurst_med_toast_%284541065102%29.jpg?utm_source=en.